# Programming languages and their tool chains, preinstalled on every desktop
# image and therefore on every system installed from it. All from Debian main.
#
# Deliberately left out:
#   php       — the metapackage pulls in the Apache web server; php-cli is the
#               language without a running web server.
#   swift     — in Debian that is OpenStack Swift (object storage). The Swift
#               language is swiftlang.
#   database servers (postgresql, mariadb-server) — they run as services
#               listening on the network. The clients and SQLite are enough to
#               write and run SQL; install a server when one is needed.

# C and C++
build-essential
clang
gdb
cmake

# Assembly (GNU as comes with binutils, via build-essential)
nasm
yasm

# Python
python3-full
python3-pip
python3-venv
python3-dev

# JavaScript / Node.js
nodejs
npm

# Go
golang-go

# Rust
rustc
cargo

# Ruby
ruby-full

# Lua
lua5.4
luarocks

# PHP
php-cli
composer

# Swift
swiftlang

# Kotlin (and the Java runtime and compiler it needs)
default-jdk
kotlin

# SQL
sqlite3
postgresql-client
mariadb-client
